plan.description:
`BuildFooter` takes `collapsed`, as `ThemeFooter` does, and a `BuildInfo`:

```ts
interface BuildInfo {
  /** The service, as its package.json names it: `@tickets/web`. */
  name: string;
  /** `0.3.2`, or `0.3.2+3` three commits past its tag. */
  version: string;
  releasedAt?: string;
  deployedAt?: string;
  commit: { sha: string; url?: string };
  branch?: string;
  environment: 'production' | 'preview' | 'dev';
  /** Dev only: the tree has uncommitted changes. */
  dirty?: boolean;
  /** Each version since the previous deploy, newest first. */
  notes: { version: string; body: string; url?: string }[];
  /** The stack's other services, as deployed with it. */
  services: { name: string; version: string; changed: boolean }[];
  /** bh's packages in this build. */
  packages: { name: string; version: string }[];
}
```

Expanded, one line: the version and the date, relative within a week; at rail width an icon whose tooltip says the same. A click opens a popover above it: the version, released, deployed, the commit (copyable, linked), the branch, the notes, the services deployed with it with those that changed marked, and bh's packages folded. Copy details puts all of it, with the browser, on the clipboard for a ticket. Tests, and a page in the shell's docs.
